  "note": "Recorded by hand from https://docs.aws.amazon.com/directoryservice/latest/admin-guide/regions.html before the parser was written. The first table has one row per Region and one Yes/No column per directory type, so each directory type is counted as its own feature. I read the 38 data rows of that table and, for each of the four directory-type columns, put every Yes Region in coveredIds and every No Region in excludedIds. 27 + 11 = 38 for Hybrid Edition and 6 + 32 = 38 for Simple AD, which is the row count, so no row was dropped. The Region column (the code) is what I resolved; the Endpoint column is a hostname and the Protocol column is always HTTPS, so neither states coverage. The second table on the page is AWS Directory Service Data (service ds-data, endpoints ds-data.*). It is a different IAM service but it is still Region coverage stated on this page, so it is counted here as its own feature on serviceId ds-data. I read its 18 data rows: the AWS Managed Microsoft AD column is Yes in all 18; the AD Connector and Simple AD columns are No in all 18, so neither can be a feature (a feature with an empty covered list is not allowed). On the Europe (Ireland) row the Simple AD cell renders the affirmative icon beside the word \"No\"; I read the word, which is what src/core/markdown.ts yesNo does and what identity-center-managed-applications does with the same conflict.",
